{"agent":"fleet-fixes-i","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The new refusal text tells the caller to run `ddflow claim {item_id} --force`:\n\n```\nf\"its {cfg.lease.grace_s}s grace period; it can be taken over \"\nf\"(`ddflow recover --item {item_id}`, then `ddflow claim {item_id} --force`) \"\n```\n\n`claim` has no `--force` flag — as the change's own intent statement records (\"claim --force is not an option, release --force is\") and as D-lease-break-explicit records (\"an idle contended lease is broken only by `ddflow claim --break`\"). Concrete scenario: holder H's lease on item T1 is past TTL, inside grace; a second agent runs `ddflow claim T1`, hits this branch, and copies the printed command. `ddflow claim T1 --force` exits with an unknown-option error, so the agent is still stuck with no way forward — exactly the symptom the bug is supposed to remove. The message must name `--break` (and/or the auto-break config) instead of a non-existent `--force`. [D-lease-break-explicit]","digest":"551f6a9e24d5ba50","location":"ddflow/services/leases.py:287 (the new grace-period branch of `acquire`)","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/services/leases.py:287 (the new grace-period branch of `acquire`)"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"The message promises automatic takeover after the grace window elapses: `in {cfg.lease.grace_s + left:.0f}s`. With the project default `[lease].break_on_timeout = false` (D-lease-break-explicit), nothing breaks the lease when the grace runs out; a later claimant still cannot take an idle contended lease without the explicit `ddflow claim --break`. So for the default configuration the printed countdown is false — an agent can sit waiting past the advertised time and still be refused. Either the branch should only print the countdown when automatic break is enabled, or it should state that `--break` is required. [D-lease-break-explicit]","digest":"f8aa55566b56633d","location":"ddflow/services/leases.py:290 (the \"can be taken over in Ns\" countdown)","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/leases.py:290 (the \"can be taken over in Ns\" countdown)"}],"chunks_total":1,"coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":2348,"diff_sha":"55a426e08a5340b51681bc8de369d5127d827c3a293ad8bbecefff84d68df744","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":48.8,"family":"deepseek","findings":2,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","output_digest":"4df4c049f7a61ca9","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-Bc99060b8ca.rubber_duck.lan-deepseek-v4.1-flash.20261017T202244Z-d6cfde4c.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1],"reviewed_head":"c52352d669d37928ce762ec1cdcfbdb98bc1f650","reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewer_digest":"d34b8af1b4a590b5","round":1,"rounds":1,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/services/leases.py:287 (the new grace-period branch of `acquire`)","ddflow/services/leases.py:290 (the \"can be taken over in Ns\" countdown)"],"tree_sha":"c52352d669d3+clean","unreviewed":[],"waves":1},"gate":"rubber_duck","reason":"2 finding(s)"},"id":"ec952f7dd0a20d360f7d1a56f","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":76852,"schema":1,"subject":"fix-Bc99060b8ca","ts":"2026-10-17T20:23:33.940854Z"}
