{"agent":"fleet-fixes-i","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The new \"way forward\" the message advertises is not runnable: it tells the user to run `ddflow claim {item_id} --force`, but `--force` is not an option on `claim` (`release --force` is; the documented explicit break path is `ddflow claim --break`). Input that demonstrates it: a holder has a lease 76s past its TTL and still inside the grace window, a second party runs `ddflow claim T1` and gets the new text `... (`ddflow recover --item T1`, then `ddflow claim T1 --force`) in Ns`. Acting on it, `ddflow claim T1 --force` fails at argument parsing with an \"unrecognized arguments: --force\" error, so the message replaces one dead end (the `-76s` countdown) with another dead end. This also contradicts the recorded decision [D-lease-break-explicit], which states that an idle contended lease is broken only by `ddflow claim --break` (automatic breaking is off by default); the message never mentions `--break`, and by default the lease is *not* \"taken over\" when the grace window elapses, so the promise \"it can be taken over ... in {grace_s + left}s\" is itself only true if the user first uses the break path. Note also that the change leaves the refusal itself untouched — `acquire` still raises for the expired-in-grace lease — so if the bug report is that the claim refuses, only the wording changed. The regression test in tests/test_lease_api.py:81 asserts the message contains `grace period` and `ddflow recover --item T1` but never checks that the suggested command is a valid invocation, so it passes on a message that cannot be followed.","digest":"89d0c41d3d38c018","location":"ddflow/services/leases.py:292 (the new grace-period message)","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/leases.py:292 (the new grace-period message)"}],"chunks_total":1,"coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":2348,"diff_sha":"55a426e08a5340b51681bc8de369d5127d827c3a293ad8bbecefff84d68df744","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":34.9,"family":"deepseek","findings":1,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","output_digest":"87045aac3ae0febc","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-Bc99060b8ca.critic.lan-deepseek-v4.1-flash.20261017T202412Z-b67ef5b7.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1],"reviewed_head":"c52352d669d37928ce762ec1cdcfbdb98bc1f650","reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewer_digest":"d34b8af1b4a590b5","round":1,"rounds":1,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/services/leases.py:292 (the new grace-period message)"],"tree_sha":"c52352d669d3+clean","unreviewed":[],"waves":1},"gate":"critic","reason":"1 finding(s)"},"id":"e23082e1d03cb8101a23e44e4","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":76868,"schema":1,"subject":"fix-Bc99060b8ca","ts":"2026-10-17T20:24:47.290640Z"}
